// shader-differential - fixture for FILE-SCOPE CONST PROMOTION (t_3bf3ce95).
//
// The reference compiler turns a file-scope `const float K = ...;` into a
// real container parameter named K whose const slots carry the initialiser;
// ours folds K to a literal.  The director's decision: both behaviours
// behind a flag, then compare.  This shader is staged three times
// (reference-pairs-const-mode.txt), each row answering one question:
//   --promote-file-consts     uniform_set=auto  the parameter is real and
//                                               patchable (both sides
//                                               patched with the same value)
//   --promote-file-consts     uniform_set=0     the COMPILED DEFAULT carries
//                                               the initialiser, not a zero
//                                               (review-found row: a promoted
//                                               name with a 0.0 default
//                                               passes the auto row)
//   --no-promote-file-consts  uniform_set=0     the fold equals the reference
//                                               compiled default
//
// Channels are chosen so each mechanism is visible on its own channel:
//   R  uv.x * K   K reaching a varying product (level count > 1)
//   G  K          the constant itself, one level whose 8-bit value IS the
//                 default (0.3125 -> 80); a zero default reads 0 here
//   B  uv.y * K   the other varying axis, same product
//   A  1
// K = 0.3125 = 5/16 is exact in float32.  The stager prints the auto value
// the promote/auto row patches in; it must differ from 0.3125 or that row
// proves nothing (it is 0.125 + m/2^24, and 5/16 needs one exact m).
const float K = 0.3125;

float4 main(float2 uv : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR
{
    return float4(uv.x * K, K, uv.y * K, 1.0);
}
